{"tool_name":"biobeam","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"biobeam","home":"https://maweigert.github.io/biobeam/","summary":"Multiplexed wave-optical simulations of light-sheet microscopy.","addition_date":"2018-07-07T17:36:55Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:46:33.372858Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:biobeam","credit":[{"email":"kreysing@mpi-cbg.de","name":"Moritz Kreysing","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://maweigert.github.io/biobeam/intro.html"},{"type":["Other"],"url":"https://maweigert.github.io/biobeam/installing.html"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://maweigert.github.io/biobeam/basic.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"},{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"}]}],"name":"Biobeam","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"migle_sur","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1006079","metadata":{"abstract":"Sample-induced image-degradation remains an intricate wave-optical problem in light-sheet microscopy. Here we present biobeam, an open-source software package that enables simulation of operational light-sheet microscopes by combining data from 105\u2013106multiplexed and GPU-accelerated point-spread-function calculations. The wave-optical nature of these simulations leads to the faithful reproduction of spatially varying aberrations, diffraction artifacts, geometric image distortions, adaptive optics, and emergent wave-optical phenomena, and renders image-formation in light-sheet microscopy computationally tractable.","authors":[{"name":"Bundschuh S.T."},{"name":"Kreysing M."},{"name":"Myers E.W."},{"name":"Subramanian K."},{"name":"Weigert M."}],"citationCount":24,"date":"2018-04-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS Computational Biology","title